# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 41 AND 42 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 9 — CHAPTER 11, 2026-09-20; the one run): 41 on 11:13 (the study before the deed,
# "which I command you", "to love", "to serve Him" as study and as prayer, the plural against 6:5 — twenty rows), 42 on 11:14 (the rain in its season, the
# early and the late, the grain gathered — ten rows); EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch11_ink.SP_; the middot checked in MIDDOT.md before
# they were typed; the rows read before marked REREAD WHOLE. Chapter 6's form.
from ch11_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(41, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IT SHALL BE, IF YOU HEARKEN DILIGENTLY TO MY COMMANDMENTS" (11:13) — WHY SAID? SINCE "YOU SHALL LEARN THEM AND KEEP TO DO THEM" (5:1), MIGHT THEY NOT BE BOUND TO STUDY UNTIL BOUND TO THE DEED? "IF YOU HEARKEN DILIGENTLY" TELLS THAT THEY WERE BOUND TO STUDY AT ONCE. The head row of piska 41 — THE SECOND PARAGRAPH\'S OPENING ({SP_(41, 1, "מגיד", "שמיד", "נתחיבו", "בתלמוד")} "it tells that they were bound to study at once"): "hearken" read as study, before the deed; 5:1 cited by name (its "learn" the qal of the consonants 11:19 reads as "teach" — computed). Read before at chapter 5 (the decalogue\'s head), REREAD WHOLE here. No code (the sequence of obligation read from two verses).')
srow(41, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'ONLY THE COMMANDMENTS BEFORE THE ENTRY — THE FIRSTBORN, THE OFFERINGS, THE CATTLE TITHE? THOSE AFTER — THE OMER, THE DOUGH-OFFERING, THE TWO LOAVES, THE BREAD OF THE PRESENCE — FROM "IF YOU HEARKEN": TO INCLUDE THE OTHER COMMANDMENTS. The inclusion ({SP_(41, 2, "לרבות", "שאר", "מצוות")} "to include the other commandments"); the Tosefta Menachot 6:20 in the English\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(41, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'ONLY BEFORE THE CONQUEST AND SETTLEMENT? AFTER — GLEANINGS, THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF, THE CORNER, TITHES, HEAVE-OFFERING, SABBATICALS AND JUBILEES — "IF YOU HEARKEN": TO ADD THE OTHER COMMANDMENTS. The second inclusion ({SP_(41, 3, "להוסיף", "עליהם", "מצוות", "אחרות")} "to add other commandments to them"). Fresh.')
srow(41, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL LEARN THEM AND KEEP TO DO THEM" (5:1) — THE DEED DEPENDS ON STUDY, NOT STUDY ON THE DEED; AND SO HE PUNISHED FOR STUDY MORE THAN FOR THE DEED: "THE LORD HAS A QUARREL WITH THE LAND\'S DWELLERS, FOR THERE IS NO TRUTH, NO KINDNESS, NO KNOWLEDGE OF GOD IN THE LAND" (HOSEA 4:1). Study first ({SP_(41, 4, "שמעשה", "תלוי", "בתלמוד")} "that the deed depends on study"; {SP_(41, 4, "שענש", "על", "התלמוד", "יותר", "מן", "המעשה")} "that He punished for study more than for the deed"): the rule of 41:11-13 stated (Kiddushin 40b the docket\'s). Read before at chapter 5, REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(41, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"NO TRUTH" — NO WORDS OF TRUTH ARE SPOKEN: "BUY TRUTH AND DO NOT SELL" (PROVERBS 23:23). ({SP_(41, 5, "אין", "דברי", "אמת", "נאמרים")} "no words of truth are spoken"). Fresh.')
srow(41, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'"NO KINDNESS" — NO WORDS OF KINDNESS ARE SPOKEN: "YOUR KINDNESS, O LORD, FILLS THE EARTH" (PSALM 119:64). ({SP_(41, 6, "אין", "דברי", "חסד", "נאמרים")} "no words of kindness are spoken"). Fresh.')
srow(41, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'"NO KNOWLEDGE" — NO WORDS OF KNOWLEDGE ARE SPOKEN: "MY PEOPLE ARE DESTROYED FOR LACK OF KNOWLEDGE" (HOSEA 4:6). ({SP_(41, 7, "אין", "דברי", "דעת", "נאמרים")} "no words of knowledge are spoken"). Fresh.')
srow(41, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'"AS THE TONGUE OF FIRE DEVOURS STRAW" (ISAIAH 5:24) — IS THERE STRAW THAT DEVOURS FIRE? THE STRAW IS WICKED ESAU: WHENEVER ISRAEL SLACKENS ITS HAND FROM THE COMMANDMENTS, HE RULES THEM. ({SP_(41, 8, "קש", "זה", "הוא", "עשו", "הרשע")} "this straw is wicked Esau"). Fresh.')
srow(41, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHO IS THE WISE MAN … WHY IS THE LAND PERISHED? — BECAUSE THEY FORSOOK MY TORAH" (JEREMIAH 9:11-12). ({SP_(41, 9, "על", "עזבם", "את", "תורתי")} "because they forsook My Torah"). Fresh.')
srow(41, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'"FOR THREE TRANSGRESSIONS OF JUDAH … BECAUSE THEY DESPISED THE TORAH OF THE LORD" (AMOS 2:4). ({SP_(41, 10, "על", "מאסם", "את", "תורת")} "because they despised the Torah of"). Fresh.')
srow(41, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'R. TARFON, R. AKIVA AND R. YOSE THE GALILEAN RECLINING AT BEIT ARIS IN LOD — WHICH IS GREATER, STUDY OR DEED? R. TARFON: THE DEED. R. AKIVA: STUDY. ALL ANSWERED: STUDY, FOR STUDY LEADS TO THE DEED. The dispute and its verdict ({SP_(41, 11, "מי", "גדול", "תלמוד", "או", "מעשה")} "which is greater, study or deed"; {SP_(41, 11, "שהתלמוד", "מביא", "לידי", "מעשה")} "for study leads to the deed"): Kiddushin 40b\'s seat (the docket\'s at 9b); no citation in either file (asserted among the eleven). Fresh.')
srow(41, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: STUDY IS GREATER, FOR IT PRECEDED THE DOUGH-OFFERING BY FORTY YEARS, THE TITHES BY FIFTY-FOUR, THE SABBATICALS BY SIXTY-ONE, THE JUBILEES BY A HUNDRED AND THREE. THE CLOCK ROW ({SP_(41, 12, "שקודם", "לחלה", "ארבעים", "שנה")} "for it preceded the dough-offering by forty years"; {SP_(41, 12, "וליובלות", "מאה", "ושלש")} "and the jubilees by a hundred and three"): the years from the giving at Sinai — the dough-offering due at the entry (forty), the tithes after the conquest and division (fourteen more — fifty-four), the sabbatical after seven years of tenure (sixty-one), the jubilee after forty-nine (a hundred and three): THE CONQUEST SEVEN AND THE DIVISION SEVEN inside the arithmetic — a DATA row for the clock (Seder Olam 11 the docket\'s; the English\'s note the computation). Fresh.')
srow(41, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'AS HE PUNISHED FOR STUDY MORE THAN THE DEED, SO HE REWARDS STUDY MORE THAN THE DEED: "YOU SHALL TEACH THEM TO YOUR CHILDREN" (11:19) — AND THEN? "THAT YOUR DAYS BE MULTIPLIED" (11:21); "HE GAVE THEM THE LANDS OF NATIONS … THAT THEY KEEP HIS STATUTES" (PSALM 105:44-45). The reward\'s measure ({SP_(41, 13, "נתן", "שכר", "על", "התלמוד", "יותר", "מן", "המעשה")} "He gave reward for study more than for the deed"): the chapter\'s own 11:19 and 11:21 the proof (the English cites both; the Hebrew quotes without a citation — the range of 40:6\'s kin). Fresh.')
srow(41, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH I COMMAND YOU TODAY" — HOW DO YOU SAY THAT ONE WHO HEARS A WORD FROM THE LEAST OF ISRAEL SHOULD HOLD IT AS FROM A SAGE? "WHICH I COMMAND YOU": AND NOT AS FROM A SAGE BUT FROM SAGES — "THE WORDS OF THE WISE ARE AS GOADS" (ECCLESIASTES 12:11), THE GOAD DIRECTING THE COW TO ITS FURROW; NOT FROM SAGES BUT FROM THE SANHEDRIN — "MASTERS OF ASSEMBLIES", "GATHER ME SEVENTY MEN" (NUMBERS 11:16); NOT FROM THE SANHEDRIN BUT FROM MOSES — "GIVEN FROM ONE SHEPHERD", "MOSES HIS PEOPLE" (ISAIAH 63:11); NOT FROM MOSES BUT FROM THE ALMIGHTY — "ONE SHEPHERD", "SHEPHERD OF ISRAEL" (PSALM 80:2), "HEAR, O ISRAEL, THE LORD OUR GOD, THE LORD IS ONE" (6:4). The ladder of five ({SP_(41, 14, "מפי", "קטן", "שבישראל")} "from the mouth of the least of Israel"; {SP_(41, 14, "כשומע", "מפי", "הגבורה")} "as one hearing from the mouth of the Almighty"): the creed\'s verse the last rung (read at chapter 6 on 6:4 and reread whole here); the sound-plays (assemblies / gather) named, no code. Read before at chapter 6, REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(41, 15, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOUR EYES ARE POOLS IN HESHBON BY THE GATE OF BATH-RABBIM" (SONG 7:5) — "YOUR EYES" THE ELDERS SET OVER THE PUBLIC (ISAIAH 29:10); "POOLS" — NONE KNOWS WHAT IS IN THEM, NONE FATHOMS THE WORDS OF THE SAGES; "HESHBON" — RECKONINGS FINISHED IN COUNSEL, IN THE HOUSES OF STUDY; "YOUR NOSE AS THE TOWER OF LEBANON FACING DAMASCUS" — IF YOU DO THE TORAH, HOPE FOR ELIJAH, "GO BACK TO THE WILDERNESS OF DAMASCUS" (1 KINGS 19:15), "REMEMBER THE TORAH OF MOSES" (MALACHI 3:22-24). The allegory of the eyes ({SP_(41, 15, "אלו", "זקנים", "המתמנים", "על", "הצבור")} "these are the elders appointed over the public"; {SP_(41, 15, "קוו", "לאליהו")} "hope for Elijah"). Fresh.')
srow(41, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO LOVE THE LORD YOUR GOD" — LEST YOU SAY: I STUDY TORAH TO BECOME RICH, TO BE CALLED RABBI, TO RECEIVE REWARD IN THE WORLD TO COME — "TO LOVE": ALL YOU DO, DO ONLY FROM LOVE. Love the motive ({SP_(41, 16, "לא", "תהו", "עושים", "אלא", "מאהבה")} "do it only from love"): 32:1\'s "act from love" (chapter 10\'s outside row) the kin; 48:12 repeats the rule on 11:22. Fresh.')
srow(41, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND TO SERVE HIM" — THIS IS STUDY. YOU SAY STUDY, OR IS IT THE ALTAR\'S SERVICE? "THE LORD GOD TOOK THE MAN AND SET HIM IN THE GARDEN OF EDEN TO WORK IT AND TO KEEP IT" (GENESIS 2:15) — WHAT WORK AND WHAT KEEPING WERE THERE THEN? "TO WORK IT" IS STUDY, "TO KEEP IT" THE COMMANDMENTS: AS THE ALTAR\'S SERVICE IS CALLED SERVICE, SO STUDY IS CALLED SERVICE. Service as study ({SP_(41, 17, "זה", "תלמוד")} "this is study"; {SP_(41, 17, "כך", "תלמוד", "קרוי", "עבודה")} "so study is called service"): I2 (the verbal analogy on "service" — checked); Eden\'s "to work it and keep it" read as study and commandments (the Genesis sitting\'s row — read at gen_08 and reread whole here).')
srow(41, 18, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND TO SERVE HIM" — THIS IS PRAYER. YOU SAY PRAYER, OR THE ALTAR\'S SERVICE? "WITH ALL YOUR HEART AND WITH ALL YOUR SOUL" — IS THERE A SERVICE IN THE HEART? SO "TO SERVE HIM" IS PRAYER: "LET MY PRAYER BE SET AS INCENSE BEFORE YOU" (PSALM 141:2), DANIEL KNEELING THREE TIMES (DANIEL 6:11), "YOUR GOD WHOM YOU SERVE CONTINUALLY" (6:21) — WAS THERE A SERVICE IN BABYLON? AS THE ALTAR\'S SERVICE IS CALLED SERVICE, SO PRAYER IS CALLED SERVICE. THE SERVICE OF THE HEART ({SP_(41, 18, "זו", "תפלה")} "this is prayer"; {SP_(41, 18, "וכי", "יש", "עבודה", "בלב")} "and is there a service in the heart"): I2 (the same analogy on "service" — checked), the heart\'s clause deciding — TA\'ANIT 2A\'S SEAT (the rain\'s mention in the prayer, the docket\'s at 9b). Fresh.')
srow(41, 19, 'CONTEXT', f'R. ELIEZER BEN JACOB: "TO SERVE HIM WITH ALL YOUR HEART AND WITH ALL YOUR SOUL" — A WARNING TO THE PRIESTS THAT THEIR HEART BE NOT DIVIDED AT THE HOUR OF THE SERVICE. ({SP_(41, 19, "אזהרה", "לכהנים")} "a warning to the priests"). Fresh.')
srow(41, 20, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: WHY "WITH ALL YOUR HEART AND WITH ALL YOUR SOUL" — IS IT NOT SAID "WITH ALL YOUR HEART AND WITH ALL YOUR SOUL" (6:5)? THERE THE INDIVIDUAL, HERE THE COMMUNITY; THERE STUDY, HERE THE DEED. SINCE YOU HAVE HEARD — DO! YOU HAVE DONE WHAT IS ON YOU, I TOO WILL DO WHAT IS ON ME: "AND I WILL GIVE THE RAIN OF YOUR LAND IN ITS SEASON" (11:14). THE PLURAL AGAINST THE SINGULAR ({SP_(41, 20, "להלן", "ליחיד", "כאן", "לצבור")} "there to the individual, here to the community"; {SP_(41, 20, "אף", "אני", "אעשה", "מה", "שעלי")} "I too will do what is on Me"): E10 (the repeated expression read — checked; the register\'s finding: 6:5\'s singular seven in the book, 11:13\'s plural four — computed); THE SHELF READS GOD\'S "I WILL GIVE" AS THE ANSWER TO ISRAEL\'S DEED — the first person the ink measured (11:14-15 God\'s weqatal in Moses\' mouth). Read before at chapter 6 (on 6:5), REREAD WHOLE here.')

srow(42, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND I WILL GIVE" (11:14) — I, NOT BY AN ANGEL AND NOT BY A MESSENGER. "THE RAIN OF YOUR LAND" — AND NOT THE RAIN OF ALL LANDS; "WHO GIVES RAIN ON THE FACE OF THE EARTH AND SENDS WATERS ON THE FACE OF THE FIELDS" (JOB 5:10). The head row of piska 42 ({SP_(42, 1, "אני", "לא", "על", "ידי", "מלאך")} "I, not by an angel"; {SP_(42, 1, "ולא", "מטר", "כל", "הארצות")} "and not the rain of all the lands"): THE FIRST PERSON READ AS GOD\'S OWN HAND (the Haggadah\'s and the Mekhilta\'s formula in the English\'s note), the suffix "your land" read to exclude other lands (40:1\'s "for its sake, all lands with it" the balance); no code. Fresh in both files.')
srow(42, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. NATHAN: "IN ITS SEASON" — FROM SABBATH NIGHT TO SABBATH NIGHT, AS IN THE DAYS OF QUEEN SHELAMZION. AND WHY SO MUCH? RABBI: SO AS NOT TO GIVE THE WORLD AN OPENING TO SAY "HERE IS THE REWARD OF ALL THE COMMANDMENTS" — RATHER "IF YOU WALK IN MY STATUTES … I WILL GIVE YOUR RAINS IN THEIR SEASON" (LEVITICUS 26:3-4), "IF YOU HEARKEN … I WILL GIVE THE RAIN OF YOUR LAND IN ITS SEASON, THE EARLY AND THE LATE" (11:13-14). The season\'s measure ({SP_(42, 2, "מלילי", "שבת", "ללילי", "שבת")} "from Sabbath night to Sabbath night"; {SP_(42, 2, "שלמצו", "המלכה")} "Shelamzion the queen"): the fold\'s Leviticus 26:3-4 set beside 11:13-14 by the shelf itself — THE TWO RAIN CLAUSES PAIRED (the compile\'s CALL at 9b), the queen\'s reign the datum (Ta\'anit 23a the docket\'s). Fresh.')
srow(42, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'ONE BLESSING WAS GIVEN TO ISRAEL IN WHICH ALL BLESSINGS ARE CONTAINED — "THE LOVER OF SILVER IS NOT SATISFIED WITH SILVER" (ECCLESIASTES 5:9), "THE ADVANTAGE OF A LAND IN EVERYTHING IS A KING SERVED BY THE FIELD" (5:8): THE KING RULES TREASURIES OF SILVER AND GOLD BUT IS BOUND ONLY TO WHAT COMES FROM THE FIELD. ({SP_(42, 3, "ברכה", "אחת", "לישראל")} "one blessing to Israel"); the Sifra parallel in the note. Fresh.')
srow(42, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"THE EARLY RAIN" (YOREH) — IT COMES DOWN AND INSTRUCTS (MOREH) MEN TO BRING IN THEIR FRUITS, PLASTER THEIR ROOFS, DO ALL THEIR NEEDS; ANOTHER WORD: IT AIMS AT THE EARTH AND DOES NOT FALL IN FURY; ANOTHER: IT COMES DOWN AND SOAKS THE EARTH TO THE DEEP — "WATERING HER FURROWS, SETTLING HER RIDGES" (PSALM 65:11). The name for its sound thrice ({SP_(42, 4, "שיורד", "ומורה", "את", "הבריות")} "that it comes down and instructs the creatures"; {SP_(42, 4, "ואינו", "יורד", "בזעף")} "and does not come down in fury"); no code (the paronomasia named). Fresh.')
srow(42, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'THE EARLY RAIN IN MARHESHVAN AND THE LATE RAIN IN NISAN — OR THE EARLY IN TISHRI AND THE LATE IN IYYAR? "IN ITS SEASON": MARHESHVAN AND NISAN; "I WILL BRING DOWN THE RAIN IN ITS SEASON" (EZEKIEL 34:26). OR AS THE EARLY RAIN KNOCKS DOWN FRUIT, WASHES SEED, FLOODS THRESHING FLOORS? "THE LATE RAIN" — AS THE LATE FOR A BLESSING SO THE EARLY; OR AS THE LATE BRINGS DOWN HOUSES, UPROOTS TREES, RAISES LOCUSTS? "THE EARLY" — AS THE EARLY FOR A BLESSING SO THE LATE; "HE HAS GIVEN YOU THE EARLY RAIN IN RIGHTEOUSNESS" (JOEL 2:23). THE SEASONS ({SP_(42, 5, "יורה", "במרחשון", "ומלקוש", "בניסן")} "the early rain in Marheshvan and the late in Nisan"; {SP_(42, 5, "מה", "מלקוש", "לברכה", "אף", "יורה", "לברכה")} "as the late rain is for a blessing so the early"): THE RAINS\' MONTHS a DATA row for the clock (Ta\'anit 6a the docket\'s — the three early rains; Mishnah Ta\'anit 1:1-3); the two rains read by each other (the mutual teaching — no code typed; the registry\'s pair rule not among the codes checked). Fresh.')
srow(42, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL GATHER YOUR GRAIN, YOUR WINE AND YOUR OIL" — YOUR GRAIN FULL, YOUR WINE FULL, YOUR OIL FULL. OR "YOU SHALL GATHER" BECAUSE THE FRUITS ARE FEW? "YOUR THRESHING SHALL REACH THE VINTAGE" (LEVITICUS 26:5) — THRESHING JUXTAPOSED TO VINTAGE: AS THE VINTAGE, ONCE BEGUN, CANNOT BE LEFT, SO THE THRESHING. The full triad ({SP_(42, 6, "דגנך", "מלא", "תירושך", "מלא", "יצהרך", "מלא")} "your grain full, your wine full, your oil full"; {SP_(42, 6, "מקיש", "דיש", "לבציר")} "it juxtaposes threshing to vintage"): the fold\'s Leviticus 26:5 the proof again (the shelf\'s second pairing of the chapter with Leviticus 26); the juxtaposition named, no code (E28\'s family is the preceding verse, not a clause pair). Fresh.')
srow(42, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: THAT YOU PLOW AT HARVEST TIME AND HARVEST AT PLOWING TIME — "AND DEW LIES ALL NIGHT ON MY HARVEST" (JOB 29:19). ({SP_(42, 7, "חורש", "בשעת", "קציר")} "plowing at harvest time"). Fresh.')
srow(42, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND YOU SHALL GATHER YOUR GRAIN" — WHY SAID? SINCE "THIS BOOK OF THE TORAH SHALL NOT DEPART FROM YOUR MOUTH" (JOSHUA 1:8), MIGHT I TAKE IT LITERALLY? "YOU SHALL GATHER" — THE TORAH SPOKE THE WAY OF THE WORLD: R. YISHMAEL. R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: THERE IS NO END TO IT — HARVEST AT HARVEST, PLOW AT PLOWING, THRESH IN THE HEAT, WINNOW IN THE WIND: WHEN DOES A MAN STUDY? RATHER, WHEN ISRAEL DOES HIS WILL THEIR WORK IS DONE BY OTHERS — "STRANGERS SHALL STAND AND FEED YOUR FLOCKS" (ISAIAH 61:5); WHEN NOT, BY THEMSELVES, AND OTHERS\' WORK BY THEM — "YOU SHALL SERVE YOUR ENEMY" (28:48). THE DISPUTE OF THE GRAIN ({SP_(42, 8, "דרך", "ארץ", "דברה", "תורה")} "the Torah spoke the way of the world"; {SP_(42, 8, "אין", "לדבר", "סוף")} "there is no end to the matter"; {SP_(42, 8, "מלאכתם", "נעשית", "על", "ידי", "אחרים")} "their work is done by others"): the verse\'s "you shall gather" against Joshua 1:8\'s "not depart" — BERAKHOT 35B\'S SEAT (the docket\'s at 9b); chapter 8\'s 28:48 cited by CALL. Fresh.')
srow(42, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: THAT THE LAND OF ISRAEL BE FULL OF GRAIN, WINE AND OIL, AND ALL LANDS FLOW TO FILL IT WITH SILVER AND GOLD — "JOSEPH GATHERED ALL THE SILVER" (GENESIS 47:14), "AS YOUR DAYS, SO YOUR STRENGTH" (33:25). ({SP_(42, 9, "מלאה", "דגן", "תירוש", "ויצהר")} "full of grain, wine and oil"). Fresh.')
srow(42, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "YOUR GRAIN" LITERALLY, "YOUR WINE" THE WINE (ISAIAH 65:8), "YOUR OIL" THE OIL (JOEL 2:24); ANOTHER WORD: YOUR GRAIN YOURS, YOUR WINE YOURS, YOUR OIL YOURS — NOT AS "WHEN ISRAEL HAD SOWN, MIDIAN CAME UP" (JUDGES 6:3) BUT AS "I WILL NO MORE GIVE YOUR GRAIN AS FOOD TO YOUR ENEMIES" (ISAIAH 62:8-9). The piska\'s close ({SP_(42, 10, "דגנך", "לך", "תירשך", "לך", "יצהרך", "לך")} "your grain yours, your wine yours, your oil yours"): the suffix read as ownership; Judges 6:3-4 the run\'s counter-case (the Judges walk\'s). Fresh.')

